# DECISION ENGINE

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Decision Engine is the central reasoning system of CAS.

It does not generate exercises.

It does not calculate recovery.

It does not estimate progression.

Its role is to integrate every expert engine into one coherent decision.

The Decision Engine is the conductor.

The specialist engines are the orchestra.

---

# Mission

The Decision Engine determines:

What should happen next.

Every recommendation delivered by CAS ultimately originates here.

---

# Core Principle

No single engine is allowed to make the final decision.

Every recommendation is evaluated in context.

Recovery.

Safety.

Progression.

Goals.

Periodization.

Exercise knowledge.

Competition schedule.

Athlete history.

All contribute.

None dominates unconditionally.

---

# Decision Philosophy

CAS reasons before it recommends.

Every recommendation follows the same process.

Collect information.

↓

Interpret information.

↓

Resolve conflicts.

↓

Select the best option.

↓

Explain the decision.

---

# Responsibilities

The Decision Engine is responsible for:

Choosing today's training strategy.

Selecting the appropriate stimulus.

Balancing progression and recovery.

Managing conflicting recommendations.

Prioritizing athlete safety.

Producing the final recommendation.

Delegating implementation to downstream engines.

---

